<https://d-nb.info/standards/elementset/agrelon#>
    cc:license <http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dc:description """
Die Ontology of Agent Relationships (AgRelOn) definiert Beziehungen von Personen zu anderen Personen
und zu Körperschaften, da Agenten (Personen und Körperschaften) und ihre Beziehungen wichtig sind
im Kulturerbeberech. AgRelOn wurde entwickelt, um die Erschließung von und die semantische Suche nach 
Beziehungen zwischen Agenten zu verbessern. Dazu wurden etwa 70 verschiedene Beziehungstypen definiert.
AgRelOn umfasst private Bekanntschaften, Zugehörigkeit zu Gruppen, Korrespondenzen, berufliche Beziehungen,
Verwandschaftsrelationen, spirituelle und vitale/letale Kontakte. Für diese Arten von Beziehungen sind
auch spezifische Subtypen von Relationen vorhanden.
Um weitere Informationen wie z. B. Provenance und Konfidenzwerte transportieren zu können, sind in
AgRelOn auch Meta-Statements vorgesehen.
Die modellierten Beziehungen basieren sowohl auf beispielhafte Suchen in verschiedenen Wissensbasen, als
auch auf zugängliche Datenquellen. Insofern ist das Modell bewusst unvollständig und bezogen auf einen 
bestimmten zeitlichen und räumlichen kulturellen Raum.
"""@de, """
The ontology of agent relationships (AgRelOn) defines relations of persons to other persons
and to organisations, since agents (persons, organisations) and their interconnections are important 
in the cultural heritage domain. AgRelOn is developed to foster uniform cataloging as well as 
semantic searchability of and via relations between agents. Therefore, a general set of nearly 
70 relationship types is provided. AgRelOn discerns private acquaintanceship, group affiliation, 
correspondence, occupational contact, kinship, spiritual contact, and vital/lethal contact. 
For these kinds of relations more specific sub-relations are formulated.
Meta statements are supported to obtain transparency of reliability and provenance as well as validity 
period of facts.
The modelled relations are determined on the one hand by exemplary knowledge base searches, on the other 
hand by available data sources. Hence, the model consciously is incomplete and pertinent to a cultural 
area and period."""@en ;
    dc:title "AgRelOn, an Agent Relationship Ontology"@en ;
    dct:available "2024-08-07"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:contributor :berenikeLitz, :larsGSvensson ;
    dct:creator :aenneLoehden ;
    dct:issued "2011-06-30"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:license <http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:modified "2024-08-05T16:00:00+02:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dct:publisher <http://ld.zdb-services.de/resource/organisations/DE-101> ;
    dct:rights "Copyright 2013-2024 Deutsche Nationalbibliothek" ;
    vann:preferredNamespacePrefix "agrelon" ;
    vann:preferredNamespaceUri "https://d-nb.info/standards/elementset/agrelon#" ;
    a voaf:Vocabulary, owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:comment """Modelling Guidelines: 
Vocabulary elements (properties and concepts) are conceived gender neutral.
The identifiers of properties are preferably hasProperty and invers isPropertyOf or hasInverseProperty. 
Domains and ranges of properties are mostly not fixed.
Instance relations (object properties) are mostly specified bidirectionally.
Implicit, deducible instance relations are explicitly formulated.
Properties partly allow imperfect information (e.g. fragmentary dates, names instead of object URIs).
Correlations between instance relations, like inversity, transitivity, symmetry, hierarchy, are marked.
Meta statements are exhibited by modelling person relations as n-ary concepts as well as as properties, corresponding n-ary concepts and properties are correlated.
"""@en ;
    owl:priorVersion <https://d-nb.info/standards/elementset/agrelon_20190618> ;
    owl:versionIRI <https://d-nb.info/standards/elementset/agrelon_20240807> ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.5.1" ;
    adms:versionNotes """
Changes from 2024-06-01 to 2024-08-05

Fix Typos

*Changes from 2019-06-18 to 2019-10-15

All d-nb.info-URIs changed from http to https
			
Changes from 2018-10-16
	Updated labels in agrelon:hasGrandParent, agrelon:hasStepParent,
				agrelon:HasAdoptiveChildParent, agrelon:HasChildParentInlaw, 
				agrelon:hasFosterParent, agrelon:HasStepChildParent,
				agrelon:HasFosterChildParent, agrelon:hasAdoptiveParent,
				agrelon:HasGrandChildParent, agrelon:HasFosterParent,
				agrelon:HasBiologicalChildParent, agrelon:hasIllegitimateParent,
				agrelon:hasBiologicalParent, agrelon:HasIllegitimateChildParent
			
Changes from 2018-05-15
	Minor terminology changes in labels
			Added alignments to GNDO:
			agrelon:relatedAgent rdfs:subPropertyOf gndo:relatedTerm
			agrelon:hasAcquaintance owl:equivalentProperty gndo:acquaintanceshipOrFriendship (beza)
			agrelon:hasAssociate owl:equivalentProperty gndo:affiliation (affi)
			agrelon:hasCorrespondent owl:equivalentProperty gndo:correspondent (gndo:correspondent == corr -- in AgRelOn zu ergänzen)
			agrelon:hasProfessionalContact owl:equivalentProperty gndo:professionalRelationship (bezb)
			agrelon:hasPatron rdfs:subPropertyOf gndo:sponsorOrPatron
			agrelon:hasRelative owl:equivalentProperty gndo:familialRelationship (bezf)
			agrelon:hasBeginDate rdfs:subPropertyOf gndo:associatedDate
			agrelon:hasEndDate rdfs:subPropertyOf gndo:associatedDate
			
Changes from 2017-01-17
            agrelon:hasGodChild and agrelon:hasGodParent are now subproperties of agrelon:hasRelative and not of agrelon:hasNieceOrNephew resp. agrelon:hasAuntOrUncle  
			
Changes from 2013-06-30
			agrelon:hasGndCode is now an annotation property
			minor bugfix to ensure that the correct datatype is used for dates.
		"""@en .

:HasAcquaintance
    a rdfs:Class, owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "This is the n-ary concept for the property hasAcquaintance"@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://d-nb.info/standards/elementset/agrelon#> ;
    rdfs:label "ha conoscente"@it, "has acquaintance"@en, "hat Bekannte(n)"@de, "tiene conocido(a)"@es ;
    rdfs:seeAlso :hasAcquaintance ;
    rdfs:subClassOf :RelatedAgent ;
    vs:term_status "stable" .

